---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About — Anywell"
			description="Anywell is a Swiss startup making civic education approachable for everyone — bite-size lessons on referendums, cantons, and how Switzerland actually works."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />

		<div class="about-hero">
			<div class="container">
				<span class="eyebrow">Our mission</span>
				<h1>Civic education should be for everyone</h1>
			</div>
		</div>

		<main class="container container--narrow">
			<div class="prose">
				<p class="lead">
					Switzerland votes on referendums three or four times a year. Citizens decide on laws,
					constitutional amendments, and budget decisions — at the federal, cantonal, and municipal
					level. That's remarkable. It's also genuinely difficult to follow if nobody ever explained
					how it works.
				</p>

				<p>
					Anywell started from a simple observation: most civics education happens in school, once,
					and is quickly forgotten. Adults who moved to Switzerland as adults, seniors who never had
					formal instruction, new citizens preparing for naturalization, parents who want to explain a
					vote to their kids — all of them deserve a clear, patient, encouraging way to learn.
				</p>

				<h2>What we're building</h2>

				<p>
					We're building a learning app — and this blog — that teaches Swiss civic fundamentals in
					small, self-contained lessons. Think of it as the friendly version of your country's
					constitution. Each lesson is 3–5 minutes, covers one idea clearly, and is followed by a
					short quiz so you actually remember it.
				</p>

				<p>
					The experience borrows the best of language-learning apps: streaks, XP, encouraging
					feedback. But the soul is distinctly Swiss — alpine, unhurried, and clear.
				</p>

				<h2>Our principles</h2>

				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Plain language first.</strong> Civic terms like "optional referendum" or "popular
						initiative" get explained in everyday words before we use the official label.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>All-ages accessible.</strong> We use Atkinson Hyperlegible — a typeface designed
						for people with low vision — for body text. Tap targets are never smaller than 48px.
						Examples speak to voters, newcomers, and retirees, not just students.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Encouraging, not patronizing.</strong> Getting a question wrong means "Not quite
						— let's look again." Getting it right means "Exactly right." We celebrate effort; we
						never shame mistakes.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Honest about Switzerland.</strong> We explain the system as it works in practice
						— including its quirks — not as a simplified fairytale. Respect for the learner means
						giving them the real picture.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>The team</h2>

				<p>
					Anywell is a small team based in Zürich. We're researchers, educators, and designers who
					believe a functioning democracy requires informed citizens — and that informed citizens
					deserve good tools.
				</p>

				<p>
					This blog is where we think out loud about civic education, accessible design, and what
					it means to build technology for the public good.
				</p>

				<div class="about-cta">
					<a href="/blog" class="btn btn-primary">Read the blog</a>
					<a href="https://github.com/Anywell-Software" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline">GitHub</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.about-hero {
		background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--violet-50) 0%, var(--violet-100) 100%);
		padding: var(--space-12) 0 var(--space-10);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
	}
	.about-hero h1 {
		margin-top: var(--space-3);
		color: var(--violet-900);
		max-width: 600px;
	}

	.lead {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--text-body);
		line-height: var(--leading-normal);
		margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
	}

	.about-cta {
		display: flex;
		gap: var(--space-3);
		margin-top: var(--space-10);
		flex-wrap: wrap;
	}
</style>
